From acf83fa0a30f49fb01dd2d9c04d12b1ea3c4d48f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:56:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] feat(providers): support native tool calls while
 streaming

This is nullclaw PR #971 (vernonstinebaker), carried here until it is merged
upstream. Drop this patch from the stack once #971 lands on main.

Decouple native tool-call support from the streaming path. Previously the
agent loop disabled native tools whenever a stream callback was attached,
forcing tools into a prompt-injection format that some models could not
reliably emit. The streaming protocol (StreamChunk / StreamChatResult) also
had no field to carry tool calls, so even if a provider parsed them they were
dropped at the agent boundary.

- providers/root: `tool_calls` on StreamChatResult, a model-aware
  `supports_streaming_native_tools` / `supports_streaming_native_tools_for_model`
  vtable capability (default false), and `freeChatResponse`.
- providers/sse: a ToolCallAccumulator that reassembles `delta.tool_calls`
  across SSE chunks, tracks `saw_arguments`, and only executes a call when the
  stream ended cleanly (`tool_calls_trusted`).
- providers/{openai,compatible}: opt in to streaming native tools;
  anthropic reports false (streaming tool-use has a different event shape).
- providers/{router,reliable}: resolve the requested model before answering
  the capability, mirroring the existing `supports_vision_for_model` precedent.
- agent/root: gate native tools on the capability when streaming and propagate
  `stream_result.tool_calls` into the agent loop.
- session: release the full vision-probe response (fixes a startup leak).
